Z||000000||-=shame=-||10-17-2001||05:54 PM||||Like I said, I have two problems. The first one, being the more annoying one, is the hard cold start. I'm going to check codes in a minute here; so I'll have more info soon. Basically, I have to try to turn it over and it will catch on the third try; after I've heard "sumthin" kick in, sounds kinda like switching the heater on with the flaps moving in the dash, it will turn over.<BR>Secondly, I work in a machine shop and can probably get the headlight motor to work just fine, but I would like a bit of a walk-through as to getting it in and out. Blah Blah <BR>thankz <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-17-2001||06:14 PM||||Problem 1)  Just a couple of ideas...  Perhaps fuel pump relay has failed, and it waits for the oil pressure switch to turn the fuel pump on?  One of the terminals in the ALDL connects to the fuel pump supply; could verify using a test light (no cost test).  If it's a V6, might want to verify the cold start injector gets energized when cranking (another no cost test).<P>Problem 2)  Use a 10mm socket + ratchet + extension.  Remove two upper nuts from the headlight assembly, raise headlight (turn on HLs, or unplug motor and hand crank,  then unplug motor if it ain't already ).  Loosen but don't remove two lower nuts.  Lower headlight assembly.  Pull headlight assembly out.           ||||reg||1
